w|scent|v|почуять, учуять|to notice something by smell or feeling|The dog scented a rabbit.|||
w|fling|v|швырнуть, бросить|to throw something with force|She flung her coat on the chair.|||
w|yell|v|орать, кричать|to shout very loudly|The coach yelled at the players.|||
w|complain|v|жаловаться|to say that you are not happy about something|He always complains about the food.|||
w|grab|v|схватить|to take something suddenly|She grabbed her bag and ran.|||
w|wrap|v|обернуть, завернуть|to cover something with paper or cloth|He wrapped the gift in blue paper.|||
w|peer|v|всматриваться, вглядываться|to look closely at something|She peered through the window.|||
w|stare|v|пристально смотреть, пялиться|to look at something for a long time|Don't stare at people.|||
w|swallow|v|глотать, проглотить|to move food down your throat|He swallowed the pill with water.|||
w|nasty|adj|неприятный, мерзкий|very unpleasant|That's a nasty cut on your hand.|||
w|silly|adj|глупый, дурацкий|not sensible|Don't be silly!|||
w|thin|adj|тонкий; худой|not thick or fat|She has a thin face.|||
